source: tests/help_snapshots.rs
expression: out
---
Emit a shell completion script for the chosen shell.

Installation (examples):
  Bash:  ubertool completions bash > /etc/bash_completion.d/ubertool
  Zsh:   ubertool completions zsh > ~/.zsh/completions/_ubertool
  Fish:  ubertool completions fish > ~/.config/fish/completions/ubertool.fish

Usage: ubertool completions [OPTIONS] <SHELL>

Arguments:
  <SHELL>
          Target shell
          
          [possible values: bash, elvish, fish, powershell, zsh]

Options:
      --json
          Output as JSON to stdout. Human messages still go to stderr

  -q, --quiet
          Bare values only (pipe-friendly)

  -v, --verbose
          Verbose progress to stderr

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version
